    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="0984" n="972" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg972"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 PW/11–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-19">November 19,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received November 19—11:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>147. Orders were issued by the Supreme Commander to the Japanese Government under
                    date of November 17 to effect the arrest of persons listed in our 121, November
                        13<anchor n="6" xml:id="d710-f1"/> except Itagaki and Yamada who are
                    understood to be out of the country. According to press, Matsuoka recently
                    attempted suicide.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d710-f1" n="6" xml:id="d710-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see despatch 52, November 13, <ref target="#pg961">p.
                    961</ref>.</p>
            </note>
